## Summary

- introduces a closed Collector failure taxonomy outside the health-state owner;
- makes unknown exceptions fatal by default;
- permits retries only for controlled SQLite contention, database-gate signals, or explicitly wrapped adapter failures;
- changes Collector health persistence and logging to accept only bounded failure codes;
- routes clipboard maintenance, clipboard polling, and adapter clipboard lifecycle failures through the same policy;
- adds taxonomy and privacy-boundary contracts.

## Root cause

`collector_health` previously inspected raw exceptions and SQLite messages, which crossed the privacy boundary and made most unknown exceptions retry indefinitely.

## Validation

The PR remains Draft until the final non-skip checkpoint passes Standard CI on an unchanged head.

## Summary

Implements the bounded `OOT-MODSDK-001` native provider slice from the ShipLua SDK plan.

- integrates the current ShipLua SDK 0.3 submodule state;
- registers experimental `actor.spawn`, `actor.destroy`, and `actor.exists` descriptors for OoT;
- translates logical allowlisted actor IDs without exposing native IDs or `Actor*` pointers;
- mints opaque handles with per-mod ownership and resource limits;
- validates object dependencies and the game thread before spawning;
- invalidates owned handles on native actor destruction, mod cleanup, scene teardown, and shutdown;
- blocks `ACTOR_PLAYER` even if accidentally added to the allowlist;
- aligns embedded ShipLua targets with Shipwright's static MSVC CRT.

Initial logical actors are `en_dog` and `en_torch2`. The public `ship.actor.*` Lua bindings remain intentionally scoped to the next `MODSDK-005` PR.

## Validation

- MSVC Release `soh` build passed and produced `x64/Release/soh.exe`.
- `oot_actor_provider_tests`: 1/1 passed.
- Embedded ShipLua tools/tests link successfully with the static CRT.
- No ROM, O2R/OTR, save, state, or generated game asset is included.

## Stack

This draft targets `agent/OOT-LINK-003-runtime` because it depends on the current OoT ShipLua runtime integration. The base PR already has inherited formatting/asset-generation CI failures; this PR should be evaluated for new failures relative to that base.

