## Summary

Completes P07 by connecting the production Control Center dashboard to the public local Operator API for project status and explicitly confirmed Start, Stop, and Native Host re-arm actions.

### Dashboard

- shows Bridge, Native Host, promoter, source cleanliness, source HEAD, PID and arm expiry;
- reads status asynchronously without mutating BDB;
- keeps startup read-only;
- supports a bounded 1–60 minute arm duration.

### Explicit mutations

- the only accepted actions are `start`, `stop`, and `rearm`;
- every action requires a selected prepared project, a separate click, and confirmation;
- cancellation exits before Operator API is called;
- only one bootstrap/status/control worker may be active;
- controls and project selection are disabled while an operation runs;
- every result is followed by a separate read-only status verification;
- no arbitrary shell, subprocess, network listener, direct Git, or BDB Core import is added.

### Versioned contracts

- `bdb-gui-project-status-v1` is read-only with zero mutations;
- `bdb-gui-control-result-v1` has the closed action enum and exactly one attempted mutation;
- the Control Center headless smoke remains a zero-mutation startup gate.

### Tests

- closed service catalog and exact Operator API routing;
- bounded arm duration and typed failures;
- cancellation before mutation;
- exactly one confirmed action plus final status read;
- double-click/concurrency blocking in a real Qt offscreen window;
- existing P05 and P06 regressions;
- full Bridge CI and Control Center GUI CI.

### Architecture

Adds ADR-0008. GUI remains a thin client over `bdb_operator`; the existing Windows operator remains the sole owner of lifecycle and STALE recovery.

## Gate

Keep in draft until both the complete Bridge CI matrix and Control Center GUI CI are green. Do not merge if startup mutates state, cancellation reaches Operator API, a second action can overlap the first, or the GUI gains direct process/network/Git execution.

